      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of both files. Let me write the improved test with better understandability — removing dead code (unused imports, constants, field, helper method) and adding clearer structure and comments.Now I'll compile-check the generated file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all dead code (unused imports, constants `BOUND`/`CHARSET_UTF8`, the `random` field, and the never-called `assertArrayEqualsAt` helper), and adds class-level and method-level Javadoc that explains the Base58 zero-byte encoding invariant and what each step of the round-trip assertion is verifying."
